-- ############################################################################
-- PART C — WHY 1,700 (raw Flatiron) AND 703 (GSK RWDAP) ARE BOTH RIGHT
--
-- Part B returned 1,700 patients for "2L docetaxel monotherapy". Phoebe's
-- 001_preprocess.R returns 703 for the same described population. Neither is
-- wrong: they are two different tables.
--
--   Phoebe   ->  hive_metastore.rwd_flatiron_dataproducts.rwdap_nsclc_2026m01_v1
--                the GSK analysis-ready data product   (filter lot2 == 'Docetaxel',
--                cohortn == 4; one row per patient, lot2 is a single-valued column)
--   Part B   ->  hive_metastore.clnprw_flatiron_nsclc_use.t_*_2026m01
--                the raw FHRD tables    (LineNumber = 2 AND LineName = 'Docetaxel';
--                many rows per patient per line)
--
-- THE LEADING EXPLANATION, from the protocol itself:
--   source FHRD  : advanced dx on or after 1 January 2011   (nsclc_protocol.md:61)
--   RWDAP        : advanced dx on or after 1 January 2017   (nsclc_protocol.md:143)
-- Six years of patients sit in the raw denominator and not in hers. Her own
-- script records the whole RWDAP at 71,445 patients (code.txt:372) where raw
-- t_enh_advancednsclc_2026m01 holds 121,889 -- 58.6% retention, the shape of a
-- 2011 -> 2017 cut. It reproduces across every line she counted:
--   2L 703/1700 = 41.4% | 3L 479/1039 = 46.1%
--   4L 167/371  = 45.0% | 5L  50/126  = 39.7%
-- A uniform ~41-46% across four independent lines is a PATIENT-level filter.
-- A line-definition disagreement would vary by line, and it does not.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT YET SETTLED, and what C0-C4 are for: the docetaxel lines retain
-- ~43% where the cohort as a whole retains 59%. The hypothesis is that 2L
-- docetaxel monotherapy is over-represented before 2017, because checkpoint
-- inhibitors displaced it from 2L in 2015-16, so the cutoff bites this cohort
-- harder than the average patient. C2 tests that directly. C4 tests the
-- secondary contributor: RWDAP lot2 is ONE value per patient, while Part B
-- matches ANY LineNumber = 2 row named 'Docetaxel', and 1,609 patients carry
-- 'Docetaxel,Ramucirumab' at 2L.
--
-- RUN ORDER: C0 and C1 read the RWDAP. C2-C6 read raw Flatiron. C0 alone can
-- confirm or kill the date hypothesis against Phoebe's own table.
-- ############################################################################

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C0. THE DECISIVE ONE.  Phoebe's exact cohort, broken out by the year of
--     ADVANCED DIAGNOSIS and by index year.
--
--     If the 2017 rule is live in the data product, adv_dx_year has NOTHING
--     before 2017 and the hypothesis is confirmed in one shot. If pre-2017
--     rows appear, the rule is not what removes the patients and C2-C4 carry
--     the explanation instead.
--
--     n_total here must come out at 703. If it does not, the disagreement is
--     in the filter, not in the population, and nothing downstream is valid.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SELECT year(addd)                        AS adv_dx_year,
       COUNT(*)                          AS n_patients,
       MIN(indexdt)                      AS earliest_index,
       MAX(indexdt)                      AS latest_index,
       SUM(CASE WHEN dthfl = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS n_deaths
FROM   hive_metastore.rwd_flatiron_dataproducts.rwdap_nsclc_2026m01_v1
WHERE  lot2 = 'Docetaxel'
  AND  cohortn = 4
GROUP  BY year(addd)
ORDER  BY adv_dx_year;

-- Same cohort, one row, so the totals can be checked against her script
-- (n_total = 703; n_deaths = 585, 83.2%; index range 2017-06-08 to 2025-12-24).
-- id3mosfu is the protocol's outcome-eligibility flag (index on or before
-- 3 months prior to data cutoff, nsclc_protocol.md:147). Her stated latest
-- index is 2025-12-24, which suggests that rule was NOT applied -- if
-- n_id3mosfu comes back below 703, patients with under three months of
-- follow-up are sitting in the denominator of an OS analysis.
SELECT COUNT(*)                                          AS n_total,
       SUM(CASE WHEN dthfl    = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)     AS n_deaths,
       SUM(CASE WHEN id3mosfu = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)     AS n_id3mosfu,
       SUM(CASE WHEN os IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)       AS n_missing_os,
       MIN(addd)    AS earliest_adv_dx,  MAX(addd)    AS latest_adv_dx,
       MIN(indexdt) AS earliest_index,   MAX(indexdt) AS latest_index
FROM   hive_metastore.rwd_flatiron_dataproducts.rwdap_nsclc_2026m01_v1
WHERE  lot2 = 'Docetaxel'
  AND  cohortn = 4;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C1. What cohortn actually codes, and how many docetaxel-2L patients sit
--     outside cohortn = 4.  Phoebe's comment (code.txt:220-224) reads
--     1 = Overall advNSCLC, 2 = L1+, 3 = L1m+, 4 = L2+, 5 = L3+. If patients
--     with lot2 = 'Docetaxel' appear under other cohortn values, then
--     cohortn = 4 is itself removing people and belongs in the funnel.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SELECT cohortn,
       MIN(cohort)               AS cohort_label,
       COUNT(*)                  AS n_patients_in_cohort,
       SUM(CASE WHEN lot2 = 'Docetaxel' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS n_lot2_docetaxel
FROM   hive_metastore.rwd_flatiron_dataproducts.rwdap_nsclc_2026m01_v1
GROUP  BY cohortn
ORDER  BY cohortn;

USE hive_metastore.clnprw_flatiron_nsclc_use;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C2. THE RAW SIDE OF THE SAME QUESTION.  Part B's 1,700, split by year of
--     advanced diagnosis and by year of 2L start.
--
--     Read it against C0. If roughly 59% of the 1,700 have an advanced
--     diagnosis before 2017, the date rule accounts for the whole gap on its
--     own. The pre_2017 column is the number the RWDAP never sees.
--
--     The second half is the interesting one: 2L-start year shows whether
--     docetaxel monotherapy really did collapse at 2L once checkpoint
--     inhibitors arrived in 2015-16. If it did, that is why this cohort loses
--     ~57% to a cutoff that costs the average patient only ~41%.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH lot2_doce AS (
  SELECT PatientID, MIN(StartDate) AS index_date
  FROM   t_lineoftherapy_2026m01
  WHERE  EnhancedCohort = 'AdvancedNSCLC'
    AND  LineNumber = 2
    AND  UPPER(TRIM(LineName)) = 'DOCETAXEL'
  GROUP  BY PatientID
)
SELECT year(a.AdvancedDiagnosisDate) AS adv_dx_year,
       year(c.index_date)            AS index_year,
       COUNT(*)                      AS n_patients
FROM   lot2_doce c
JOIN   t_enh_advancednsclc_2026m01 a ON a.PatientID = c.PatientID
GROUP  BY 1, 2
ORDER  BY 1, 2;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C3. THE RECONCILIATION FUNNEL.  Each step a strict subset of the last, in
--     the order the evidence supports. The last step should land near 703.
--
--     s1 -> s2  : the protocol's cohort-entry rule (adv dx >= 2017-01-01).
--                 Expect this to be the dominant single step.
--     s2 -> s3  : patients whose 2L is docetaxel and NOTHING ELSE. RWDAP lot2
--                 holds one regimen per patient; a 2L with a second segment
--                 (e.g. Docetaxel,Ramucirumab) would not read as 'Docetaxel'
--                 there but is matched by Part B.
--     s3 -> s4  : index must fall on or after the advanced diagnosis (already
--                 true for all 1,700 at B3, kept so the funnel is complete).
--     s4 -> s5  : the outcome-eligibility rule, index on or before 3 months
--                 before cutoff. SET THE CUTOFF LITERAL BELOW -- the value
--                 here is derived from the data, not assumed. If s5 lands
--                 materially below 703, the rule was not applied in her 703.
--
--     A residual after s5 is NOT failure; it is the size of what is still
--     unexplained, and worth reporting as such rather than tuning away.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH cutoff AS (          -- derive rather than assume the data cut
  SELECT GREATEST(
           (SELECT MAX(StartDate)     FROM t_lineoftherapy_2026m01),
           (SELECT MAX(DiagnosisDate) FROM t_diagnosis_2026m01)
         ) AS data_cutoff
),
lot2_rows AS (
  SELECT PatientID, LineName, StartDate
  FROM   t_lineoftherapy_2026m01
  WHERE  EnhancedCohort = 'AdvancedNSCLC'
    AND  LineNumber = 2
),
lot2_doce AS (
  SELECT PatientID, MIN(StartDate) AS index_date
  FROM   lot2_rows
  WHERE  UPPER(TRIM(LineName)) = 'DOCETAXEL'
  GROUP  BY PatientID
),
lot2_doce_only AS (       -- the patient's ENTIRE 2L is docetaxel, no other regimen
  SELECT PatientID
  FROM   lot2_rows
  GROUP  BY PatientID
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT UPPER(TRIM(LineName))) = 1
     AND MAX(UPPER(TRIM(LineName))) = 'DOCETAXEL'
),
base AS (
  SELECT c.PatientID,
         c.index_date,
         a.AdvancedDiagnosisDate,
         (o.PatientID IS NOT NULL) AS doce_only_2l
  FROM   lot2_doce c
  JOIN   t_enh_advancednsclc_2026m01 a ON a.PatientID = c.PatientID
  LEFT   JOIN lot2_doce_only o         ON o.PatientID = c.PatientID
)
SELECT (SELECT data_cutoff FROM cutoff)                                AS derived_data_cutoff,
       COUNT(*)                                                        AS s1_partB_1700,
       SUM(CASE WHEN AdvancedDiagnosisDate >= DATE'2017-01-01'
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)                                     AS s2_adv_dx_2017plus,
       SUM(CASE WHEN AdvancedDiagnosisDate >= DATE'2017-01-01'
                 AND doce_only_2l
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)                                     AS s3_2L_is_docetaxel_only,
       SUM(CASE WHEN AdvancedDiagnosisDate >= DATE'2017-01-01'
                 AND doce_only_2l
                 AND index_date >= AdvancedDiagnosisDate
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)                                     AS s4_index_after_adv_dx,
       SUM(CASE WHEN AdvancedDiagnosisDate >= DATE'2017-01-01'
                 AND doce_only_2l
                 AND index_date >= AdvancedDiagnosisDate
                 AND index_date <= add_months((SELECT data_cutoff FROM cutoff), -3)
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)                                     AS s5_three_month_followup
FROM   base;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C4. How much of the gap the regimen-string difference alone can carry.
--     Part B's 1,700 counts a patient whose 2L holds a 'Docetaxel' segment
--     even when it also holds another. This shows the overlap explicitly:
--     if n_doce_plus_other is large, Part B's monotherapy filter is looser
--     than the RWDAP's and the number needs qualifying wherever it is quoted.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH lot2_rows AS (
  SELECT PatientID, UPPER(TRIM(LineName)) AS ln
  FROM   t_lineoftherapy_2026m01
  WHERE  EnhancedCohort = 'AdvancedNSCLC'
    AND  LineNumber = 2
)
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT PatientID)                                       AS n_any_docetaxel_2L_row,
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN n_regimens = 1 THEN PatientID END)     AS n_docetaxel_only_2L,
       COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN n_regimens > 1 THEN PatientID END)     AS n_doce_plus_other,
       MAX(n_regimens)                                                 AS max_regimens_at_2L
FROM  (SELECT PatientID,
              COUNT(DISTINCT ln)                                       AS n_regimens,
              MAX(CASE WHEN ln = 'DOCETAXEL' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)        AS has_doce
       FROM   lot2_rows
       GROUP  BY PatientID) t
WHERE has_doce = 1;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C5. B4 RE-RUN WITHOUT NODAL, AND AS THREE STATES.
--
--     Two corrections to B4, both required before the site count is used.
--
--     (a) NODAL DROPPED. B5 put lymph_node second at 275 patients. Optum's
--         curated table excludes nodal involvement by vendor definition, so
--         C77 / 196 must come out before the two sources are compared at all.
--
--     (b) THREE STATES, NOT A COUNT. B4 found only 55.6% with any pre-index
--         site code. In a 2L advanced cohort essentially everyone has
--         metastatic disease, so a coded zero is overwhelmingly NOT CODED
--         rather than no disease -- and ICD cannot express absence, which is
--         exactly what Optum's mets_qualifier = 'absent' adds. So the honest
--         states off ICD are: sited (a specific compartment is coded),
--         unspecified (a secondary-neoplasm code exists but names no site --
--         C79.9 / 199.0), and not_coded (no secondary-neoplasm code at all).
--         Model the three states; do not model the count.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH lot2_doce AS (
  SELECT PatientID, MIN(StartDate) AS index_date
  FROM   t_lineoftherapy_2026m01
  WHERE  EnhancedCohort = 'AdvancedNSCLC'
    AND  LineNumber = 2
    AND  UPPER(TRIM(LineName)) = 'DOCETAXEL'
  GROUP  BY PatientID
),
dx AS (
  SELECT d.PatientID,
         CASE
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.5%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.5%' THEN 'bone'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.7%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.7%' THEN 'liver'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.3%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.3%'
             OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.4%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.4%' THEN 'brain_cns'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.0%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.0%' THEN 'lung'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.2%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.2%' THEN 'pleura'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.7%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.7%' THEN 'adrenal'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.6%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.6%' THEN 'peritoneum'
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.9%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '199.0%' THEN NULL
           WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78%'   OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79%'
             OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197%'   OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198%'   THEN 'other_organ'
           ELSE NULL
         END AS site_group,
         -- any secondary-neoplasm code at all, nodal deliberately EXCLUDED
         CASE WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79%'
                OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198%'
                OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '199.0%'
              THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS any_secondary_code
  FROM   t_diagnosis_2026m01 d
  JOIN   lot2_doce c ON c.PatientID = d.PatientID
  WHERE  d.DiagnosisDate < c.index_date            -- strictly pre-index: no leakage
),
per_pt AS (
  SELECT c.PatientID,
         COUNT(DISTINCT dx.site_group)                AS n_met_sites,
         COALESCE(MAX(dx.any_secondary_code), 0)      AS has_any_secondary
  FROM   lot2_doce c
  LEFT   JOIN dx ON dx.PatientID = c.PatientID
  GROUP  BY c.PatientID
)
SELECT CASE WHEN n_met_sites > 0        THEN 'sited'
            WHEN has_any_secondary = 1  THEN 'unspecified'
            ELSE                             'not_coded' END           AS site_state,
       COUNT(*)                                                        AS n_patients,
       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) / SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 1)              AS pct,
       ROUND(AVG(n_met_sites), 2)                                      AS mean_sites_in_state,
       SUM(CASE WHEN n_met_sites >= 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)               AS n_with_3plus
FROM   per_pt
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY n_patients DESC;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- C6. B5 without nodal, so the compartment mix is Optum-comparable.
--     Compare the shape against Optum's Part A vocabulary, NOT the rates:
--     Optum's 24.4% is over all notes-eligible lung patients at any stage,
--     Part B's 55.6% is over 1,700 patients already at 2L of advanced
--     disease. Different denominators. The comparison that does hold is
--     sites per captured patient -- Optum 2.6, Flatiron ICD 1.8 -- which says
--     the ICD proxy under-counts sites even inside the patients it captures.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH lot2_doce AS (
  SELECT PatientID, MIN(StartDate) AS index_date
  FROM   t_lineoftherapy_2026m01
  WHERE  EnhancedCohort = 'AdvancedNSCLC'
    AND  LineNumber = 2
    AND  UPPER(TRIM(LineName)) = 'DOCETAXEL'
  GROUP  BY PatientID
)
SELECT CASE
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.5%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.5%' THEN 'bone'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.7%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.7%' THEN 'liver'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.3%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.3%'
           OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.4%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.4%' THEN 'brain_cns'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.0%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.0%' THEN 'lung'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.2%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.2%' THEN 'pleura'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.7%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198.7%' THEN 'adrenal'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78.6%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197.6%' THEN 'peritoneum'
         WHEN d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79.9%' OR d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '199.0%' THEN 'unspecified_site'
         ELSE 'other_organ'
       END                         AS site_group,
       COUNT(DISTINCT d.PatientID) AS n_patients
FROM   t_diagnosis_2026m01 d
JOIN   lot2_doce c ON c.PatientID = d.PatientID
WHERE  d.DiagnosisDate < c.index_date
  AND  ((d.DiagnosisCodeSystem = 'ICD-10-CM' AND (d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C78%' OR
                                                  d.DiagnosisCode LIKE 'C79%'))
    OR  (d.DiagnosisCodeSystem = 'ICD-9-CM'  AND (d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '197%' OR
                                                  d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '198%' OR
                                                  d.DiagnosisCode LIKE '199.0%')))
  -- NODAL DELIBERATELY ABSENT: no C77, no 196. Optum excludes nodal by definition.
GROUP  BY 1
ORDER  BY n_patients DESC;

-- ############################################################################
-- READING PART C
--   C0  adv_dx_year has nothing before 2017  -> the RWDAP date rule is live
--       and is the explanation. n_total must be 703 or the filter disagrees.
--   C2  pre-2017 share of the 1,700          -> how much of the gap it carries
--   C3  s5 near 703                          -> funnel closed; a residual is
--       the size of what remains unexplained and should be reported, not tuned
--   C4  n_doce_plus_other large              -> Part B's 1,700 is a looser
--       monotherapy definition than Phoebe's and must be quoted as such
--   C5  not_coded share                      -> why site COUNT is unusable off
--       ICD; report the three states instead
--   C6  compartment mix, nodal removed       -> the only Optum-comparable form
--
-- WHICH NUMBER SHOULD PHOEBE USE?  703 is the right one for anything that has
-- to sit inside the RWDAP protocol, and it is the one her covariates exist for.
-- 1,700 matters because it is the ceiling: it says the 2017 rule, not data
-- scarcity, is what bounds this cohort, and that a protocol amendment rather
-- than a different data source is what would grow it.
-- ############################################################################
